Outline of the Sediment Disaster Prevention Act
Designation of sediment disaster hazard zones [prefectures]
(Areas where sediment disasters are likely to occur)
* Official name: Act on Promotion of Sediment Disaster Countermeasures in Sediment Disaster Hazard Areas
The Sediment Disaster Prevention Act* is intended to promote non-structural measures to protect people’s lives from sediment
disasters, including the dissemination of information on areas potentially endangered by sediment disasters, improvement of alert
and evacuation systems, restriction of new housing and land development and promotion of the relocation of existing houses.
Guidelines on sediment disaster risk management [MLIT]
Implementation of basic investigation [prefectures]
· Basic policies on measures to prevent sediment disasters
· Implementation guidelines for basic investigation
· Designation guidelines for sediment disaster hazard zones
